            <ArticleTitle>Stenting of unprotected left main coronary artery in a patient with cardiogenic shock.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-304</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 64-year-old female presented with pulmonary edema and cardiogenic shock after coronary arteriography that showed severe subocclusive lesion in the left main coronary artery (LMCA) in a dominant left coronary system. The patient successfully underwent urgent angioplasty with stent deployment in the LMCA. After an uneventful period, the patient was discharged at day six.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
